Validate the pairlist chain before load() restores it into an environment.

RestoreToEnv() (src/main/saveload.c) receives whatever R_Unserialize()
or the pre-1.4 readers produced and only checks that the head is a
pairlist node (isList()).  It then walks CDR() to the end, taking
TAG() and CAR() of every node as a symbol and its value.  A
hand-crafted .RData file can splice any object into the chain: the
fuzzer put an external pointer there, whose CAR slot is its (NULL)
address, so defineVar() bound a NULL SEXP and the pre-2.4.0 S4 check
dereferenced it.

    ==6788==ERROR: AddressSanitizer: SEGV on unknown address 0x000000000000
        #0 Rf_isObject               src/main/memory.c:4794
        #1 R_seemsOldStyleS4Object   src/main/objects.c:1801
        #2 RestoreToEnv              src/main/saveload.c:2224
        #3 R_LoadSavedData           src/main/saveload.c:2236

Other object types in the CDR position fare no better: vectors are read
as pairlist nodes through their length fields (a NULL dereference), and
a fresh symbol loops forever, since its value slot is R_UnboundValue,
whose own value slot is itself.  Reject a chain that holds anything but
LISTSXP nodes with symbol tags, with the existing "not in pair list
form" error.
Both load() entry points (loadFromConn2 for RD?2/RD?3 files and the
.Internal(load()) fallback) go through RestoreToEnv().

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #393 and Bugzilla 19238 (attachment
3936), filed 2026-10-21.  The PR also
adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R), not carried here.
Found by the load target: oss-fuzz testcase 4654451810697216
(2026-10-19).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/saveload.c
+++ b/src/main/saveload.c
@@ -2132,7 +2132,13 @@ static SEXP RestoreToEnv(SEXP ans, SEXP aenv)
 
     PROTECT(ans);
     a = ans;
-    while (a != R_NilValue) {a = CDR(a); cnt++;}
+    while (a != R_NilValue) {
+	/* a hand-crafted file can splice any object into the chain */
+	if (TYPEOF(a) != LISTSXP || TYPEOF(TAG(a)) != SYMSXP)
+	    error(_("loaded data is not in pair list form"));
+	a = CDR(a);
+	cnt++;
+    }
     PROTECT(names = allocVector(STRSXP, cnt));
     cnt = 0;
     a = ans;
